# JACKAL — black-backed jackal top-down, FRONT=UP, stalking. CANINE essentials from above:
# a smooth long body oval (heavily-overlapped circles — visible segments read larva/insect),
# a clear NECK NARROWING, a snout protruding well past the skull, ears flanking with a gap,
# the dark saddle FRONT-LOADED over the shoulders (the black-backed identifier), a bushy
# slightly-angled black-tipped tail. Menace: lean + low head + bared forward fangs.
#
# --- FUR + LIMBS, APPLIED (ref assets/sprites/ref/fur/jackal_canis_mesomelas) ---
# FUR: the body Circles are value-graded (one continuous radial, lit shoulders -> shadow hips);
# the COAT is `Lock` strokes (the brush, formal/draw.md): a dark saddle wash for the mantle's
# mass, then short locks laid from the hips FORWARD so each shingles over the roots behind it
# — dark over the shoulders fanning outward and thinning to the hips, a transition row fading
# it into the tan, tufts only at the silhouette (irregular, tips past the circle edge), and a
# tufted tail with its black tip as a dark lock. Implied, never a wig; the first asset drawn
# with the brush, and the render is byte-identical through draw.py and the loft `drawing`
# library.
# LIMBS: two SHORT forelegs reach FORWARD alongside the snout, each a clawed paw — kept forward
# not splayed so it reads canine, not insect (the Canis mesomelas plate is the form reference).
# Source for assets/sprites/jackal.png.
size 256x256
Background transparent
# the one footprint every Lock below drags — a Brush must precede its locks
Brush fur hair w=12 period=36 seed=3 gap=0.3

# tail — bushy, slightly angled (dead-straight reads larval), BLACK TIP
name tail
Poly (0.50,0.68)@13 (0.535,0.82)@11 (0.525,0.93)@7 stroke=120,92,58
# tail fur — short tufts lying ALONG the tail, alternating sides, sweeping back toward the tip
# (the body's texture level, not a smooth ribbon beside a furred back), then the BLACK TIP as
# a dark lock, no wider than the tail, whose spikes end it
Lock (0.505,0.700) (0.488,0.730)~ (0.480,0.758) brush=fur w0=2 w=6 tips=2 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=41 rgb=138,108,68 dark=92,70,42 lit=176,146,100
Lock (0.532,0.745) (0.552,0.776)~ (0.560,0.804) brush=fur w0=2 w=6 tips=2 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=42 rgb=138,108,68 dark=92,70,42 lit=176,146,100
Lock (0.512,0.790) (0.498,0.822)~ (0.492,0.850) brush=fur w0=2 w=6 tips=2 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=43 rgb=130,100,62 dark=86,64,38 lit=170,140,96
Lock (0.538,0.830) (0.552,0.862)~ (0.556,0.888) brush=fur w0=2 w=5 tips=2 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=44 rgb=130,100,62 dark=86,64,38 lit=170,140,96
Lock (0.516,0.862) (0.508,0.890)~ (0.504,0.912) brush=fur w0=2 w=5 tips=2 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=46 rgb=130,100,62 dark=86,64,38 lit=170,140,96
Lock (0.527,0.895) (0.522,0.945)~ (0.516,0.995) brush=fur w0=4 w=6 tips=3 tipvar=0.4 spread=12 seed=45 rgb=34,28,24 dark=16,12,10 lit=70,60,50

# forelegs are drawn LAST (on top), reaching forward alongside the snout, so they're VISIBLE
# rather than hidden under the body (the old tucked paws were). See the forelegs block at the end.

# body — ONE smooth lean oval (closely-stacked overlapping circles, no seams)
name hips
Circle (0.50,0.575) r=0.108 radial=142,110,70>106,78,46 at=0.50,0.37,0.26
Circle (0.50,0.525) r=0.115 radial=142,110,70>106,78,46 at=0.50,0.37,0.26
name midbody
Circle (0.50,0.475) r=0.118 radial=142,110,70>106,78,46 at=0.50,0.37,0.26
Circle (0.50,0.425) r=0.115 radial=142,110,70>106,78,46 at=0.50,0.37,0.26
name shoulders
Circle (0.50,0.385) r=0.110 radial=142,110,70>106,78,46 at=0.50,0.37,0.26

# THE SADDLE — the dark mantle's MASS, a tapered dorsal wash the locks lie on
name saddle
Poly (0.50,0.390)@20 (0.50,0.475)~@15 (0.50,0.560)@7 stroke=54,44,34
# THE COAT — short LOCKS, laid from the hips FORWARD so each forward lock shingles over the
# roots behind it. The saddle is a dense cluster of dark locks over the shoulders, angles
# fanning outward, thinning to the hips; a transition row fades it into the tan; the tan
# flank stays the body's own radial, with tufts only at the SILHOUETTE — irregular (four
# left, three right, mixed lengths), angled outward-back, tips past the circle edge.
# Short and many rather than long and few: a coat is implied, never a wig.
name fur
Lock (0.472,0.600) (0.460,0.640)~ (0.450,0.670) brush=fur w0=2.5 w=8 tips=3 tipvar=0.45 spread=16 seed=1 rgb=148,118,76 dark=98,74,46 lit=186,156,108
Lock (0.530,0.602) (0.544,0.638)~ (0.556,0.664) brush=fur w0=2.5 w=7 tips=3 tipvar=0.45 spread=16 seed=2 rgb=148,118,76 dark=98,74,46 lit=186,156,108
Lock (0.482,0.542) (0.468,0.580)~ (0.456,0.610) brush=fur w0=2.5 w=9 tips=3 tipvar=0.45 spread=16 seed=3 rgb=96,76,50 dark=54,42,28 lit=138,112,76
Lock (0.518,0.538) (0.532,0.578)~ (0.544,0.612) brush=fur w0=2.5 w=8 tips=3 tipvar=0.45 spread=16 seed=4 rgb=96,76,50 dark=54,42,28 lit=138,112,76
